---
title: Bounties
description: The MonoGame Foundation uses a bounty system to propose paid incentives to improve the project.
---
{% extends "layouts/base.layout.njk" %}

{% block content %}
    <section class="mg-bounties-hero" aria-labelledby="bounties">
        <div class="container-xxl mg-bounties-hero-inner">
            <div class="mg-bounties-hero-copy">
                <nav class="mg-about-breadcrumb mg-bounties-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
                    <a href="/">Home</a>
                    <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
                    <span>Bounties</span>
                </nav>
                <h1 id="bounties">Help shape what MonoGame builds next.</h1>
                <p>
                    The <a href="/foundation/">MonoGame Foundation</a> offers paid bounties for work that moves the framework and its community forward.
                </p>
                <div class="mg-bounties-hero-actions">
                    <a class="btn btn-lg mg-button mg-bounties-primary hide-external-icon" href="https://github.com/MonoGame/MonoGame/issues/8120">
                        <i class="bi bi-github" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>View open bounties</span>
                    </a>
                    <a class="btn btn-lg mg-outline-button mg-bounties-secondary hide-external-icon" href="mailto:biz@monogame.net">
                        <i class="bi bi-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <span>Ask a question</span>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container-xxl mg-bounties-section" aria-labelledby="how">
        <div class="mg-bounties-section-heading">
            <div>
                <p class="mg-bounties-eyebrow">A straightforward process</p>
                <h2 id="how">How bounties work</h2>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mg-bounties-process-grid">
            <a class="mg-bounties-process-card hide-external-icon" href="https://github.com/MonoGame/MonoGame/issues/8120">
                <span>01</span>
                <i class="bi bi-binoculars" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <h3>Find a bounty</h3>
                <p>Review the open bounties, their scope, and the application deadline on GitHub.</p>
                <span class="mg-bounties-process-link">Browse the board <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            </a>
            <a class="mg-bounties-process-card hide-external-icon" href="mailto:biz@monogame.net?subject=Bounty%20application">
                <span>02</span>
                <i class="bi bi-send" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <h3>Send a proposal</h3>
                <p>Email your references and a proposed schedule, noting the bounty you would like to complete.</p>
                <span class="mg-bounties-process-link">Email your proposal <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            </a>
            <a class="mg-bounties-process-card" href="#requirements">
                <span>03</span>
                <i class="bi bi-patch-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <h3>Work with the Foundation</h3>
                <p>The coordinator reviews applications with the board and confirms the successful applicant publicly.</p>
                <span class="mg-bounties-process-link">Review requirements <i class="bi bi-arrow-down" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="mg-bounties-note">
            <i class="bi bi-info-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <p>Applications usually close around two weeks after a bounty opens. If no suitable application is received, the bounty remains open.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="container-xxl mg-bounties-section" aria-labelledby="requirements">
        <div class="mg-bounties-requirements">
            <div class="mg-bounties-requirements-intro">
                <p class="mg-bounties-eyebrow">Before you apply</p>
                <h2 id="requirements">Requirements for bounty applicants</h2>
                <p>We want applications to be fair, practical, and ready to move forward once a selection has been made.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="mg-bounties-requirement-list">
                <li><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-text" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>US citizens must provide a <a href="https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-form-w-9">W-9</a>; non-US citizens must provide the correct <a href="https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-form-w-8">W-8</a> when selected.</span></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-shield-check" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Your country of registration and bank must not be subject to United States commercial embargoes.</span></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-currency-dollar" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Your bank must receive USD, or a currency supported by <a href="https://wise.com/help/articles/2571942/what-countriesregions-can-i-send-to?id=2571942&slug=what-countries-can-i-send-to">Wise</a>.</span></li>
                <li><i class="bi bi-file-earmark-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>You may need to sign a service agreement and, where required, a Non-Disclosure Agreement.</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="mg-bounties-closing">Bounties are not competitions: unless stated otherwise, one applicant is selected based on their expertise and proposed schedule.</p>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
